  :adr/clarifying-answers-2026-07-15
  {:org-taxonomy
   "exactly 3 receiving-entity orgs: gftdcojp (GFTD Japan), jk-luxury (JK
    株式会社), com-junkawasaki (personal). Group by receiving entity, not by
    counterparty/vendor -- a repo per counterparty was explicitly rejected as
    excessive. Data must stay cross-referenceable by project unit and by
    contact unit from a single canonical store, not duplicated per grouping."
   :storage-visibility "one private repo under com-junkawasaki, nothing
                         pushed publicly"
   :rollout "prototype a small batch first, then expand to all 319 files"}
  :adr/investigation-findings
  {:local-manimani
   "orgs/gftdcojp/local-manimani is a mature triage app (Gmail/message inbox
    -> single-keypress policy -> mechanical follow-through), event-sourced
    JSONL ledger (1 decision = 1 git commit), web(shadow-cljs)+tauri+mobile
    clients. Its OWN domain schema (src/manimani/ds.cljc) is triage-specific
    and explicitly marked unused/slated-for-removal in its README; the
    top-level schema.edn is auto-generated cross-repo bookkeeping, unrelated
    to documents/contacts/orgs. Its Tauri companion app already visualizes
    the SIBLING m365-archive repo's ingest status -- the precedented
    integration shape for a future 'Documents' view of archive-scans."
   :m365-archive
   "hybrid DataLad dataset: raw M365 data + a derived facts/ layer
    (blobs.jsonl CID<->path<->size, messages/threads/attachments.jsonl,
    people.edn, orgs.edn, docs.jsonl, contract-terms.jsonl) atop a Datomic
    schema (datomic/schema-m365.edn, queried via `cd datomic && clojure
    -M:run`, :storage-dir :mem so plaintext DB never touches disk).
    .gitattributes forces facts/** to stay annex.largefiles=anything
    (annexed+encrypted) even though it's .edn/.jsonl, while datomic/**
    (schema/query definitions only) stays plain git. This is the exact
    template followed here."
   :datascript-npm-in-nbb-spike
   "empirically confirmed incompatible: datascript@1.7.8 (npm) is a
    Closure-advanced-compiled cljs bundle with its own internal cljs.core;
    nbb/SCI's interpreted collections don't satisfy its protocols
    (IKVReduce etc). create_conn needs a genuine JS object (clj->js) for
    schema; transact/q then either throw or silently produce empty results
    (#js []) regardless of whether tx-data/query are passed as clj->js
    objects, raw cljs forms, or EDN strings -- no combination round-tripped.
    Real querying is deferred to a genuine cljs compile (shadow-cljs, e.g.
    local-manimani's web/) where `:require [datascript.core :as d]` compiles
    against the SAME compiler and does not hit this cross-runtime wall.
    Interim: plain nbb filter/group-by helpers over facts/*.jsonl."
   :com-junkawasaki-github-account
   "confirmed via gh api users/com-junkawasaki: type=User (personal GitHub
    account owned by Jun Kawasaki), not a GitHub Organization. New repos are
    created as com-junkawasaki/<name> --private directly against that
    account, per ADR-2607021330's default (spot-checked: ghosthacker=private
    matches default, webmaster=public is a known intentional exception)."}
  :adr/schema
  {:entities [:org/id :org/name
              :contact/id :contact/name :contact/company :contact/org
              :project/id :project/name :project/org
              :blob/cid :blob/path :blob/bytes :blob/mime
              :doc/id :doc/blobs :doc/org :doc/category :doc/date
              :doc/counterparty :doc/contact :doc/project :doc/amount
              :doc/source-filename :doc/notes]
   :cid-convention "blob/cid == git-annex content key (e.g.
                    MD5E-s147511--<hash>.jpg), matching m365-archive's own
                    facts/blobs.jsonl convention -- no separate IPFS CID
                    scheme introduced"
   :file "orgs/com-junkawasaki/archive-scans/datomic/schema-archive.edn"}
  :adr/storage-split
  {:plain-git ["README.md" "bin/**" "datomic/**" "docs/adr/**" ".gitattributes"]
   :annexed-encrypted-b2 ["scans/** (raw image/pdf binaries)"
                          "facts/** (unconditional, even .edn/.jsonl -- PII
                           defense in depth, same rule as m365-archive)"]
   :b2-credential "reuses the already-provisioned 1Password item
                   com-junkawasaki.b2/annex (vault gftdcojp) -- no new
                   bucket/credential created"}
